TEST 18571 -- 802.1Q Trunk a Dynamic Aggreagator
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-09 19:56:28-20:01:49 NZDT (x230 clock: NZ local time labelled "UTC", ~3 s
          behind tb470; stack clock: true UTC, ~48 s ahead of tb470)
Bench:    tb470, consoles u0 (swi_f) and u5 (stk_a master); Test Engineer terrenceb@terrenceb-dl
Tester:   bench-runner (by hand: tools/ckcon.py via tools/tb ckcon, tools/linerate.py,
          tools/rc2cfg.py; no framework script)
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWPTCM-T18571 (Approved), objective "To confirm that the dynamic aggreagator will work as
          normally as a trunked port", precondition "change the configuration such that the
          trunked port", 1 step
Build:    swi_f awplus_main-20261008-57 (x230v2_28GS-awplus_main-20261008-57.rel, build date
          Thu Oct 8 00:10:09 UTC 2026), bootloader 6.2.40
          stk_a awplus_main-20261008-57 on members 1, 3 and 4
Configs:  swi_f.cfg, stk_a.cfg (running-config after setup; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- an 802.1Q trunk built as an LACP (dynamic) aggregator carries line-rate traffic from many source MACs with no 4-byte deficit
      LACP aggregator po12, 2 links ...... synchronized  (x230 and stack, before and after the traffic)
      1518-byte frames eth3 -> eth1 ....... PASS  (812501 / 812501 at exact length, 999.7 Mbps on the wire)
      1518-byte frames eth1 -> eth3 ....... PASS  (812501 / 812501 at exact length, 999.4 Mbps on the wire)
      1500-byte frames eth3 -> eth1 ....... PASS  (822501 / 822501 at exact length, 999.8 Mbps on the wire)
      64 source MACs over both links ...... 50/50  (x230 per-member counters, each direction)
      drops on any x230 port .............. 0
CAVEAT:  No Ixia on tb470: tools/linerate.py (tcpreplay) on tb470's 1G NICs stands in, with 64
         rotating source MACs per sender. "No 4 byte deficit" is proven end to end: every frame
         left the far access port at exactly the length sent after crossing the tagged trunk; the
         tagged frames on the trunk links themselves were not captured. Small frames and VLANs
         other than 106 were not sent.

